{"name":"Seal of Good Local Governance — BARMM passers","generatedAt":"2026-10-08","source":[{"label":"DILG — 2022 List of Seal of Good Local Governance Awardees","href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/PDF_File/reports_resources/dilg-reports-resources-20221212_edc9f21a30.pdf","year":2022},{"label":"DILG — 2023 List of Seal of Good Local Governance Awardees","href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/PDF_File/reports_resources/dilg-reports-resources-2023122_da533a136c.pdf","year":2023},{"label":"DILG — 2024 List of Seal of Good Local Governance Awardees","href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/PDF_File/reports_resources/dilg-reports-resources-20241114_3a530a4e56.pdf","year":2024},{"label":"SGLG Incentive Fund 2022 — DILG Caraga, 30 December 2022: P9.5 million provinces, P7 million cities, P5 million municipalities","href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/regional-news/DILG-Caraga-awards-incentive-funds-to-SGLG-passers-in-the-region/NR-2022-1184","year":2022},{"label":"SGLG Incentive Fund 2023 — DILG CAR, 22 January 2024: PHP 4 million provinces, PHP 2.3 million cities, PHP 1.8 million municipalities","href":"https://car.dilg.gov.ph/23-cordi-lgus-get-p44-1-m-grant-urged-to-use-incentive-fund-for-high-impact-projects/","year":2023},{"label":"SGLG Incentive Fund 2024 — Philippine Daily Inquirer, citing DILG: P3 million provinces, P2 million cities, P1,153,000 municipalities; P980,281,000 in all (41 × 3M + 96 × 2M + 577 × 1.153M reproduces it)","href":"https://newsinfo.inquirer.net/2014344/more-lgus-bag-this-years-dilg-seal-of-good-local-governance-award","year":2024},{"label":"DILG — Seal of Good Local Governance reports and resources (no 2020 or 2021 list is posted)","href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/reports-and-resources/seal-of-good-local-governance/12/"}],"note":"Which BARMM provinces, cities and municipalities DILG conferred the Seal of Good Local Governance, by assessment year, transcribed from DILG’s signed awardee lists (scans, read by OCR and checked against the page and against the BARMM count on each list’s summary page). This is a passer list only: DILG does not publish who was assessed, so an LGU missing from a year either did not pass or was not assessed — the data cannot tell which, and it is never a recorded failure. \"incentive\" is the SGLG Incentive Fund amount DILG announced for that level that year (an entitlement, not a confirmed release to that LGU; sources in \"source\"). There are no awards for 2020 (assessment suspended for COVID-19), 2021 (no awards conferred) or 2025 (assessment deferred while DILG recalibrated the SGLG); none for 2026 is published yet — see \"status\". The 2022 and 2023 lists name the province \"Maguindanao\"; it is under \"former\" because neither successor province can claim it (the 2023 list post-dates the September 2022 split and does not say which). Towns listed under \"Maguindanao\" sit under the province they are in now. Sulu (Talipao passed in 2023) is left out, as in every other dataset here. Barangay seals (SGLGB) are not here. \"bangsamoroSeal\" is a different award, by a different body: see its own note.","years":[2022,2023,2024],"status":{"2020":"No awards: the 2020 assessment was suspended for the COVID-19 pandemic; DILG posts no 2020 awardee list.","2021":"No awards: no SGLG was conferred for 2021 (reported as a pilot field test year under the SGLG Act, RA 11292); DILG posts no 2021 awardee list.","2025":"Deferred: DILG Memorandum Circular 2025-032 deferred the CY 2025 assessment while the SGLG is recalibrated.","2026":"No awardee list published as of the build date."},"units":{"basilan/lamitan":{"2022":{"passed":true,"award":"Seal of Good Local Governance 2022","incentive":7000000,"href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/PDF_File/reports_resources/dilg-reports-resources-20221212_edc9f21a30.pdf"},"2023":{"passed":true,"award":"Seal of Good Local Governance 2023","incentive":2300000,"href":"https://www.dilg.gov.ph/PDF_File/reports_resources/dilg-reports-resources-2023122_da533a136c.pdf"},"2024":{"passed":true,"award